 timecalc='<div class="tool"><label>Region <select id="medal-region">'+regionopts+'</select></label><label>Difficulty <select id="medal-tier"><option value="0">Normal</option><option value="1">Hard</option><option value="2">Nightmare</option></select></label><label>Clear time, minutes <input id="medal-minutes" type="number" min="0" max="999" value="18"></label><label>Seconds <input id="medal-seconds" type="number" min="0" max="59" value="0"></label><label><input id="medal-win" type="checkbox" checked> This was a completed Classic win</label><p id="medal-result" role="status"></p></div>'
 article('time-attack','PokeBonk Time Attack: Medal Times & Clear-Time Checker','Check a Classic clear against Time Attack medals','Check PokeBonk medal thresholds by region and difficulty, evaluate a completed Classic time, and separate personal medals from seasonal ranking rewards.','Time Attack evaluates completed Classic wins. In the checked Season 2 Normal schedule, Silver is 24:00, Gold 18:00 and Champion 13:30. Choose your region and difficulty below rather than applying Normal times to every run.'+ref(1)+ref(2),[('checker','Check a completed clear time',scope+timecalc),('thresholds','Compare region and difficulty thresholds',table(['Region','Difficulty','Silver ≤','Gold ≤','Champion ≤'],medalrows)+'<p>These are client-derived thresholds, not our gameplay timings. The checker requires a win and uses inclusive boundaries, matching the client medal function.</p>'+ref(2)),('global','Choose between another region and a faster clear','<p>The project’s Season 2 notes describe Global Time Attack as best wins across regions, prioritizing region coverage before total time. Keep region coverage and a single-map personal best as different objectives.</p><p>For an uncleared region, first establish a repeatable clear. For a known route, record avoidable detours and delays between objectives. Our tool cannot predict a finishing time from your draft.</p>'+ref(2)),('rewards','A medal is not a guaranteed seasonal prize','<p>A personal time medal and a ranked seasonal reward are separate. Rank depends on other submitted runs and the project’s review; this page does not fetch live leaderboards or claim a prize for your account.</p><p>Before chasing a seasonal payout, read the current season information and reward notice in the original game. Historical dates or older screenshots are not proof that a reward can still be earned.</p>'+ref(2))],src,[('how-to-win/','Finish Classic consistently first'),('maps/','Check region progression'),('builds/','Choose a practice route')],script='depth.js')
 # Put the useful controls before illustration; retain an original, task-specific diagram below.
